The population distribution is extremely uneven. The [[Sorres Blanques (comarca)|Sorres Blanques]] comarca, containing the provincial capital [[Novara]], accounts for approximately 50 per cent of the provincial population with a density of 7,209/km². The surrounding coastal comarcas — [[La Marina (comarca)|La Marina]], [[Els Prats (comarca)|Els Prats]], and [[La Sénia (comarca)|La Sénia]] — are the next most populous, with mixed agricultural and tourism economies. The remote northern comarcas — [[Birú Est (comarca)|Birú Est]], [[Montdarrera (comarca)|Montdarrera]], and [[Els Ports (comarca)|Els Ports]] — are the most sparsely populated, with densities below 7/km².

